# debian-ios/pins/bookworm-arm64.pins
#
# Version lock for everything the initramfs is built from. fetch-inputs.sh refuses
# to build if the archive no longer offers one of these versions (PIN DRIFT), so a
# rebuild either reproduces the documented artefact or fails loudly.
#
# The SHA-256 of every .deb is taken from the Debian archive's own index stanza at
# fetch time and verified before the file is used -- the version pin and the hash
# check are independent, and both must pass.
#
# format: <package> <version>
#
# ---- the userland that is actually requested -------------------------------------
busybox-static 1:1.35.0-4+deb12u1+b1
dash 0.5.12-2
coreutils 9.1-1
dpkg 1.21.23
sed 4.9-1+deb12u1
grep 3.8-5
tar 1.34+dfsg-1.2+deb12u1
gzip 1.12-1
# ---- pulled in by dependency resolution (sha256-verified like the rest) ----------
debianutils 5.7-0.5~deb12u1
libc6 2.36-9+deb12u14
libgcc-s1 12.2.0-14+deb12u1
gcc-12-base 12.2.0-14+deb12u1
libacl1 2.3.1-3
libattr1 1:2.5.1-4
libselinux1 3.4-1+b6
libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1
libbz2-1.0 1.0.8-5+b1
liblzma5 5.4.1-1+deb12u1
libzstd1 1.5.4+dfsg2-5
libmd0 1.0.4-2
zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1
libgmp10 2:6.2.1+dfsg1-1.1
# ---- STAND-IN QEMU kernel: NOT our A9 kernel and not part of the initramfs -------
# Used only to boot the initramfs on a virtual arm64 machine. It is a 4K-page
# Debian kernel; the A9 kernel must be built 16K (config_16k) and is built by
# kernel-engineer (task-6), not here. See debian-ios/README.md "what the smoke
# test does and does not prove".
linux-image-6.1.0-50-arm64 6.1.176-1
